  "question": {
    "text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is launched up on a rough inclined plane making an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the horizontal. The coefficient of friction between the body and plane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math> if the time of ascent is half of the time of descent. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi></math></p><p>Using the above values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></math> and putting in<br />equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math>, we will get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
